Example of heading layout:
<h1 class="O-ch-num"><span class="ch-num">CHAPTER</span> 1 <span class="O-ch-title">CH-TITLE</span></h1>

Added CSS to O-ch-title attribute:
span.O-ch-title::before{
content: '\A';
white-space: pre}

Example:
a{
text-decoration:underline;
color:inherit;
}
a.link{
text-decoration:underline;
color:inherit;
}

Example:
<p class="drop-cap">Although electricity and electrical energy was...</p>

p.drop-cap::first-letter {
color: #A52A2A;
float: left;
font-size: 5em;
margin: 0 .1em 0 0;
line-height: 0.85;
}

Example:
<h1 class="TOOL-T" id="tool01">Tools for Student and Instructor Success</h1>

.TOOL-T{
font-size:150%;
font-family:MyriadPro-Bold_fnt;
margin:1em 0em 0.25em 0em;
text-indent:0em;
text-align:left;
line-height:1.2em;
color:#fffffe;
background:#006aa6;
padding:0.5em;
text-transform:uppercase;
}

